== importQuantifiers {"owedWrappers": "every Plan-SELECTED import2 of the atom evidenceKind that is relevant to the current subject (wrapper scope intersects current logicalPath / history observational scope). NOT merely proof.evaluationInputRefs. A selected relevant wrapper omitted from evaluationInputRefs cannot hide uncertainty on negatives.", "consumable": "mapped current (StalenessRule current); unmapped-only never feeds polarity set R", "polaritySetR": {"runtime": ["observed-hit", "observable-unhit"], "neverInR": ["unobservable", "unmapped"], "observabilityFilter": "restricts matching polarity. Unobservable/unmapped rows never enter R or make exists true; otherwise relevant such rows remain disclosed as uncertain independently of the observability filter."}, "kleene": {"exists": "true if any owed consumable wrapper contributes a polarity match, even if siblings are partial/incomplete", "none": "false if any known polarity match exists, even if another wrapper is partial. True only if every OWED relevant wrapper is observationally complete AND R is empty. Else indeterminate.", "count-at-most": "false once known distinct ObservationAddress count > N, even if siblings partial. True only if every owed relevant wrapper is complete AND count <= N. Else indeterminate when count <= N.", "all-covered": "true only if every owed relevant wrapper is complete AND every selected current subject has a covering row (runtime observed-hit or observable-unhit; history in-scope subject row). Never false."}, "runtimeComplete": "wrapper.completeness=complete AND observation.window non-null AND population present AND population != unknown. This does NOT establish observability of a missing, unobservable, or unmapped subject.", "runtimeNegativeRow": "none/count-at-most true and all-covered additionally requi
